course: dictionary
lesson: 5584
title: A word that is not really a word
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some letters are not a word at all, but a piece of a longer word, a name, or a short form. «Li» is one of these. You will rarely meet it in ordinary English, so when you do, ask: is this a name, a symbol, or a piece of something else?
explain: Read the words around it. «A legend says Li Bai drowned reaching for the Moon's reflection, but he probably died of illness.» Li is the start of a person's name, because Bai is a name too and the sentence is about a man. Capital letters and the words around it are clues.
explain: The same letters can mean different things. In a science lab, Li is a symbol for the metal lithium. On a web page, the code li marks one item in a list. Look at the subject around it to decide which meaning fits, then try your meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
fact: "Li" is not a usual English word, so do not expect it in everyday sentences.
fact: In Chinese, a li is an old unit of length, about half a kilometre.
fact: Li is a common Chinese family name, as in «Mr Li» and «Li Na».
fact: The symbol Li stands for the metal lithium in science.
fact: In HTML, the code li marks one item of a list on a web page.
fact: Context tells you which meaning is right, so read the sentence before you decide.
exercise: In science, the symbol Li stands for which element? | Liquid | *Lithium, a metal | Lightning | A kind of fruit
exercise: «Mr Li» is a name for a man. What is Li doing in this name? | It is one item in a list | It is an old unit of length | It is the symbol for lithium | *It is a family name
exercise: Chinese travellers once used the li to measure a road. About how long is one li? | About ten metres | *About half a kilometre | About a hundred kilometres | About five kilometres
test: On a web page, the code «li» marks what? | *One item in a list | A link to another site | A picture | A bold heading
test: «A legend says Li Bai drowned reaching for the Moon's reflection.» What is Li part of in this sentence? | An old unit of length | The symbol for lithium | A list item on a web page | *The start of a person's name
exam: On a science chart, Li most likely means: | One item in a web page list | An old unit of length | *The metal lithium | A family name
